      "ID": "14",
      "Event Name": "Cannibalism",
      "Details": "Burial parties vanish from an army at war. Ration books are quietly changed, bodies are cut apart, and frightened soldiers whisper that officers are protecting the people responsible.\n\nThe army must feed its units, protect witnesses, and hunt organized killers without turning the whole front into a panic. Covering up the crimes keeps order briefly and gives the predators room to recruit.\n\nWhat began in hungry armies has spread through ritual cells, prison gangs, communes, islands, and armed host states. Hannibal Lecter now stands at the center of the network.\n\nFeeding territories, couriers, and regional armies follow one campaign. Surviving governments must free consumed districts, cut the routes between them, and choose which local resistance leaders can be trusted.",
      "Evo I": "Ritualized Ranks\n\nScattered predators now share oaths, marks, ranks, and protection. The cells recognize one another, though nobody can find a headquarters.",
      "Evo II": "The Organized Network\n\nCells in different countries use the same ledgers, courier routes, prisoner rules, and attack schedules. The network is clearly organized, but its center is still hidden.",
      "Evo III": "Hannibal Lecter Commands\n\nHannibal Lecter steps into public view and begins drawing the mature network into one command.",
      "Evo IV": "",
      "Evo V": "",
      "World-End Scenario": "The World Is the Larder\n\nThe last limits on Hannibal Lecter's command have been struck from its ledgers. Warlord armies, prison routes, silent ports, and feeding states answer a single timetable, carrying each conquest into the next.\n\nEvery country outside the Host has been named as prey. Its armies march in the certainty that each ruined city will furnish the next advance and each defeated population will be counted as supply.\n\nNo Thaw Will Come\n\nEvery transformation anchor has sealed beneath frost and butchered stone. The transformed Hannibal Lecter no longer depends on roads, seasons, or the living institutions that once confined his armies.\n\nCannibal Hosts and winter packs move together from the frozen capitals, drawing fresh strength from every population they overrun. The cold ahead of them carries no terms, accepts no surrender, and leaves no season in which the hunted can recover.",
      "Type": "Minor Fire-Once",
      "Chaos level": "1",
      "Cluster ID": "",
      "Status": "Needs Testing"
